{
  "id": "8f26811da62fe952",
  "name": "deploykit - retro ingest",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## deploykit - retro inlet\n\nA finished retro comes in through any of three doors and every `### Issue:` in it (plus every promoted debt entry) is triaged into Linear via the shared core.\n\n**Doors:**\n- **Form** - open the Retro Form node's URL, paste the retro. Zero extra setup.\n- **Webhook** - what the `/retro` Claude skill POSTs to (`{ customer, retro_markdown }`). Zero extra setup.\n- **GitHub** - push a `retros/*.md` file; pick owner/repo on the two GitHub nodes and add a GitHub credential. Optional.\n\n**Setup:** point *Run Issue Triage* at the imported issue-triage core, attach an OpenAI credential on the model node, activate.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333300",
      "name": "Setup Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-60, -460]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "path": "deploykit-retro-form",
        "formTitle": "Submit a deployment retro",
        "formDescription": "Paste a completed RETRO.md. Every issue in it will be deduplicated against the tracker and filed or +1'd.",
        "formFields": {
          "values": [
            {
              "fieldLabel": "Customer",
              "placeholder": "acme",
              "requiredField": true
            },
            {
              "fieldLabel": "Retro markdown",
              "fieldType": "textarea",
              "requiredField": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333301",
      "name": "Retro Form",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.formTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [0, -160]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "deploykit-retro",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333302",
      "name": "Retro Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [0, 40]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "owner": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "repository": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "events": ["push"],
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333303",
      "name": "GitHub Push",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.githubTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [0, 240],
      "credentials": {
        "githubApi": {
          "id": "CONFIGURE_ME",
          "name": "GitHub account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const payload = $json.commits ? $json : ($json.body || {});\nconst commits = payload.commits || [];\nconst files = new Set();\nfor (const c of commits) {\n  for (const f of [...(c.added || []), ...(c.modified || [])]) {\n    if (/^retros\\/.*\\.md$/.test(f)) files.add(f);\n  }\n}\nreturn [...files].map(f => ({ json: { file_path: f } }));"
      },
      "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333304",
      "name": "Changed Retro Files",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [220, 240]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "file",
        "operation": "get",
        "owner": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "repository": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "filePath": "={{ $json.file_path }}",
        "asBinaryProperty": false,
        "additionalParameters": {}
      },
      "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333305",
      "name": "Fetch Retro File",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.github",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [440, 240],
      "credentials": {
        "githubApi": {
          "id": "CONFIGURE_ME",
          "name": "GitHub account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "return $input.all().map((item, i) => {\n  const j = item.json;\n  let customer;\n  let retro;\n\n  if (j.body && (j.body.retro_markdown || j.body.customer)) {\n    // webhook: POST { customer, retro_markdown } - e.g. from the /retro skill\n    customer = j.body.customer;\n    retro = j.body.retro_markdown;\n  } else if (j['Retro markdown'] || j.Customer) {\n    // form submission\n    customer = j.Customer;\n    retro = j['Retro markdown'];\n  } else if (j.content && j.encoding === 'base64') {\n    // github file fetch (retros/YYYY-MM-DD-<customer>.md)\n    retro = Buffer.from(j.content, 'base64').toString('utf8');\n    const m = (j.path || j.name || '').match(/\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}-(.+)\\.md$/);\n    customer = m ? m[1] : 'unknown';\n  }\n\n  return { json: { customer: customer || 'unknown', retro_markdown: retro || '' }, pairedItem: i };\n}).filter((i) => i.json.retro_markdown.length > 0);"
      },
      "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333306",
      "name": "Normalize Retro",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [680, 40]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are processing a deployment retrospective into discrete, trackable issues.\n\nCustomer/deployment: {{ $json.customer }}\nRetro document:\n<<<\n{{ $json.retro_markdown }}\n>>>\n\nExtract every distinct issue:\n- Each \"### Issue:\" block is one issue - read its fields.\n- Each Debt Log entry with verdict \"promote\" in the debt review is ALSO one issue (these are platform gaps that should become roadmap items).\n- Ignore \"what worked\" items, metrics, and decisions.\n\nFor each issue produce:\n- summary: one line, root-cause oriented.\n- system: component/integration involved, or \"unknown\".\n- times_seen: integer count from the retro (default 1).\n- severity: blocker | major | minor.\n- context: self-contained sanitized context an engineer can act on - no customer-identifying data.\n- workaround: the Workaround field verbatim (typically a Debt Log link), or \"none\".",
        "hasOutputParser": true
      },
      "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333307",
      "name": "Split Into Issues",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.5,
      "position": [900, 40]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-4.1-mini"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333308",
      "name": "OpenAI Chat Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [960, 280],
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "CONFIGURE_ME",
          "name": "OpenAI account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "schemaType": "manual",
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"issues\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"summary\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"system\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"times_seen\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n          \"severity\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"blocker\", \"major\", \"minor\"] },\n          \"context\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"workaround\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"summary\", \"context\"]\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"issues\"]\n}"
      },
